{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42472 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "N-Methyltyramine is implicated in the biological activity of SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions involving dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members. These enzymes are targets of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and Phorone, which in turn target SMMC-7721. The evidence suggests that N-Methyltyramine may act as a modulator or activator of these SDR family members, which then exert their effects on SMMC-7721. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which N-Methyltyramine influences SMMC-7721, possibly through the activation of metabolic pathways that are critical for the cell's survival or proliferation. The presence of multiple targets in the SDR family and their shared effect on SMMC-7721 underscores the importance of these enzymes in the biological response to N-Methyltyramine.",
